The Director of Facilities will lead the strategy, design, and operation of PsiQuantum’s global facilities portfolio, including high-tech laboratories, cleanrooms, manufacturing spaces, data centers, and office environments.&nbsp;This executive will be responsible for ensuring all physical infrastructure supports the company’s mission to deliver scalable quantum computing systems, maintaining world-class reliability, safety, and efficiency.&nbsp;The role requires a seasoned facilities leader with deep experience in technically complex, mission-critical environments - ideally combining R&amp;D, semiconductor, and advanced manufacturing expertise.

Responsibilities:

Strategic Facilities Leadership

• Develop and implement a long-term global facilities and infrastructure strategy aligned with PsiQuantum’s growth and technical roadmap.

• Lead master planning for laboratory, cleanroom, cryogenic, and manufacturing facilities to ensure scalable capacity for quantum hardware development.

• Partner with executive leadership to evaluate site expansion, new facility builds, and real-estate acquisition.

• Establish facilities policies and standards that promote operational excellence, safety, and sustainability.

